<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Romance of the Three Kingdoms</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Sanguo yanyi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Romance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms</a> is a Chinese historical novel attributed to Luo <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanzhong">Guanzhong</a> in the 14th century, one of the four classic novels of Chinese literature. It dramatises the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> and the wars of Wei, Shu and Wu, mixing history with legend. Its portraits of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bei">Liu Bei</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guan-yu">Guan Yu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-fei">Zhang Fei</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhuge-liang">Zhuge Liang</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a> shaped how <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> remembers the period.</p></div>
